# Text is stored and checked out with LF on every platform. Git for Windows'
# default (core.autocrlf=true) checked text out with CRLF, so on Windows the
# code base differed from what every test and tool saw on Linux and macOS.
# Batch files keep CRLF: cmd.exe can mis-parse labels in LF-only batch files.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
